cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hoop Impact Bench, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Hoop Impact Bench (HIB): an open benchmark for NBA impact metrics"
version: "1.0.0"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://lumahoops.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lumahoops/hoop-impact-bench"
abstract: >
  Hoop Impact Bench scores NBA player impact metrics on one question: do the values known before a season predict
  that season? Every metric is scored on the same regular-season games (2020-21 to 2025-26) under the same rules
  (Taylor Snarr's 2020 retrodiction rules): game-margin R-squared, correlation with team win % (Krishna Narsu, 2024)
  and face-value error against opponent-adjusted team margin (Snarr, 2020), each also on rebuilt rosters, with
  bootstrap intervals and rank ranges. Bring a CSV of ratings and run one command.
authors:
  - name: "LUMA Basketball Research"
    website: "https://lumahoops.org"
  - family-names: Awoyemi
    given-names: Ayo
keywords:
  - NBA
  - basketball
  - sports analytics
  - benchmark
  - player impact metric
  - plus-minus
  - RAPM
  - retrodiction
